# Baseline hook allowlist — one grep -E pattern per line; blank lines and
# lines starting with # are ignored. A staged line matching any pattern is
# exempted from the gate that consulted it.
#
# These four entries cover CLAUDE.md §14, which teaches British English by
# showing the US spellings as "X not Y" counter-examples. The BRE gate
# correctly spots the US words; here they are deliberate teaching text, so
# they are exempted. The patterns are anchored to the "*british* not us"
# contrast so they cannot mask a real US spelling elsewhere.
\*analyse\* not analyze, \*colour\* not color
\*behaviour\* not behavior, \*recognise\* not recognize
not organization, \*licence\* \(noun\) and \*license\* \(verb\)
dictates \(e\.g\. CSS `color`, `Cargo\.toml` `license` field
